# HomTensors: plan and status

Goal: `Lax119563.WitnessFromRounds.witness_from_rounds` (paper
`framework-hom-upper-bound.tex`, Theorem `thm:witness-from-rounds`).

## Design

* `BagTree` — rooted bag trees given by parent pointers decreasing a depth. `BagTree.Valid`
  (cover, edges in a bag, equality pairs in equal or parent/child bags, unique topmost bag per
  vertex) implies a `Lax228581` tree decomposition of any graph on a quotient of the vertex set
  generated by the equality pairs (`BagTree.hasTreewidthAtMost`).
* `LGraph k` — labeled graphs with an edge relation (loops, orientation irrelevant), color
  predicates, *equality constraints* `eqv` (instead of quotienting while gluing), and `k`
  labels. `tensor`, `homCount`, `sum_tensor`. `Good F N`: a valid bag tree of width `k` with
  all labels in the root bag, and up to `eqv` at most `N` non-label vertices.
* `glue` — one generic gluing operation: fresh vertices `L` (root bag), parts `F j` whose labels
  are identified with `σ j`. Tensor formula `tensor_glue`; goodness `good_glue` with size
  `|L \ range lam| + ∑ N_j`. Specialisations: `mul` (product of tensors, size `a + b`) and
  `extG` (extension, size `1 + k N`); `atom` for graphs on the labels only (size `0`).
* `PolyClosure` — `mem_polySpan`: functions constant on agreement classes of a finite `𝒢`
  lie in the span of products of at most `|X| - 1` elements of `𝒢`.
* `Spaces` — `Vs G H N` = span of tensors of `N`-good graphs on `V(G)^k ⊔ V(H)^k`;
  `Vs_mul`, `one_mem_Vs`, `extOp_mem` (via a generic multilinearity lemma).
* `Rounds` — `ind_mem`: class indicators of round `r` lie in `Vs (ν_r)`, with `ν_0 = 0`,
  `ν_{r+1} = (M - 1)(1 + k ν_r)`. Round zero uses polynomial closure on atom tensors
  (no Möbius inversion needed).
* `Unlabel` — `exists_coloredGraph`: quotient by `eqv`, rule out loops, symmetrise edges, split
  by compatible colorings.
* `WitnessFromRounds` — the main theorem; `k + ν_r ≤ k (k M)^r` (`nu_bound`).

## Status

All files complete; see the git log of branch `proofs/homtensors`.
